  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hello. I recently got back into creating custom avatars, but after my first model using the newest SDK, all of my models have been tagged as having more than 2 BILLION polygons. As an artist who's developed for games in the past, I make it a point not to make models over 25K tris. Doing some troubleshooting I have found that the Skeletal rig may be related, as the error only starts appearing when I have marked the FBX as a Humanoid rig, but then it never goes away. I have tried re-exporting the models from Blender, reinstalling the SDK, and closing/re-opening Unity. Nothing works. I am using Unity 2017.4.28f1. If it helps with debugging this issue, I have noticed the Unity Console reports a \"stack overflow exception\" for Line 276 of AvatarPerformanceStats.cs.",
